id: pm-rust-mttg
title: Match published punctuation-bearing tag normalization order
description: "A synthetic update with tags +1,-0,.5 exposes a pre-existing ordering divergence: Rust sorts +1,-0,.5 while published PM CLI 2026.10.9 writes -0,.5,+1. This changes canonical item and history bytes independently of the toon-format upgrade. Characterize published tag normalization before changing native sorting."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: compatibility,mutation
created_at: "2026-10-10T02:46:34.001Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T06:54:45.458Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: A differential update with punctuation-bearing tags matches complete item and history bytes without weakening existing fixture comparisons.
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T02:47:20.128Z",codex-sol,"The same synthetic regression also exposes an independent history patch gap on replacing a two-tag array with eight tags: native replaces the whole tags value while the published CLI emits indexed replace/add operations. Canonical item bytes match for that fixture; complete history bytes do not. Codec regression creates its numeric-looking tag array directly so it exercises canonical encoding without hiding this separately tracked replacement-patch gap."
  "2026-10-13T12:23:42.385Z",codex-agent,"Use native ICU collation to reproduce published localeCompare ordering for trimmed and deduplicated tags; cover punctuation, mixed case and Unicode against the locked 2026.10.13 oracle."
  "2026-10-13T12:58:26.797Z",codex-agent,"The refreshed 2026.10.13 differential passed punctuation, mixed-case and Unicode tag normalization with exact item and recursive JSON-patch history bytes. Final gate execution and behavioral revert proof remain pending."
  "2026-10-13T13:15:32.355Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof passed: replacing only normalize_tags locale ordering with lexical ordering kept the harness compilable and failed the punctuation differential at runtime (exit 101, one failing test). Restored the locale normalization exactly."
  "2026-10-14T06:54:24.306Z",codex-agent,"Native ICU English tag ordering and normalized deduplication match published 2026.10.14 item/history bytes. The linked exact-name ordering differential passed through pm test: one passed, zero ignored, 15 unrelated functions filtered. A strengthened tag-only revert retained trimming/lowercasing and restored lexical sorting; punctuation order alone caused one compiled runtime regression failure (exit 101), then sources were restored byte for byte. The complete release gate passed 278 tests per toolchain without filtering, with 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches. Leaving open for orchestrator verification."
